<Project>

  <!--
    Applies to every project in this solution.

    Windows Smart App Control (Windows Security > App & browser control) refuses to load freshly
    built, unsigned DLLs, and its verdict is cached against the file's hash. A normal .NET build is
    deterministic: the same source always produces byte-identical output, so once a build has been
    blocked, rebuilding it produces the same file and stays blocked - the app then fails at startup
    with "An Application Control policy has blocked this file. (0x800711C7)" and no amount of
    rebuilding clears it.

    Turning determinism off puts a fresh identifier in each build, so every rebuild is a new file
    that gets judged afresh and the problem clears itself. Reproducible builds are not something
    this project needs, so this is a safe trade.

    If nobody in the group has Smart App Control switched on, this line can simply be deleted.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Deterministic>false</Deterministic>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
